WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:06.030
In 1882, Engelmann lit a thin strand
of alga with a spectrum of light.

2
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:10.050
Bacteria that seek oxygen
crowded into just two zones:

3
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.040
the blue and the red.

4
00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:15.660
Leaves look green because they
absorb little green light.

5
00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:18.300
Yet a leaf holds more than green pigment.

6
00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:22.240
So how can you reveal a leaf's
hidden orange and yellow pigments,

7
00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:23.840
and what are they for?

8
00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.860
In this mission, you'll meet
the pigments a leaf holds,

9
00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:30.580
and see that each one catches
a different part of the light.

10
00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:34.270
Then you'll run a classic practical,
take careful measurements,

11
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.900
and use them to name each pigment.

12
00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:40.630
Your mission: find out how to
reveal the hidden pigments,

13
00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:41.800
and what they do.
